/*! \mainpage

gr-soarr is a GNU Radio out-of-tree module implementing the ground-station
side of a CCSDS Telecommand (TC) uplink chain for ARIS's SOARR mission:
encapsulation, SDLS encryption and authentication, TC transfer framing,
pseudo-randomization, BCH encoding, and CLTU framing on TX, and the
matching detection, correction, reassembly, verification, and decryption
on RX.

All blocks are implemented in Python (namespace gnuradio.soarr), so this
Doxygen manual contains no C++ block reference. Block documentation is in
each block's Python docstring (help(soarr.<block>)) and in docs/prd/ in
the source tree; the pipeline is described in docs/architecture.md.

*/
